# sirius USB role follow: event sources (no polling timer).
# All rules call the same idempotent script (flock-protected, safe on storms).
# - extcon (ID edge) has NO rule on purpose: the gpio38 IRQ never fires on
#   this phone (verified silent with udevadm monitor), and the handler holds
#   on hid anyway, so a rule would be doubly dead. ID cables stay manual.
# - power_supply change on pm660-charger: VBUS online/offline (PC plug/unplug).
# - usb_device add/remove: peripheral enumerate/unplug (boost-leak sweep).
# - platform change with OTG_CABLE (qcom_smbx cable flip):
SUBSYSTEM=="platform", ACTION=="change", ENV{OTG_CABLE}=="?*", RUN+="/usr/local/sbin/sirius-usb-bind"
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", ACTION=="change", ENV{POWER_SUPPLY_NAME}=="pm660-charger", RUN+="/usr/local/sbin/sirius-usb-bind"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ACTION=="add", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", RUN+="/usr/local/sbin/sirius-usb-bind"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ACTION=="remove", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", RUN+="/usr/local/sbin/sirius-usb-bind"
